    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Monomorphic epitheliotropic intestinal T-cell lymphoma</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The epitheliotropic lymphoma cells in the peripheral zone are cytologically atypical, featuring medium-sized lymphoid cells with irregular nuclear contours, moderate nuclear pleomorphism, more open chromatin, and distinct nucleoli.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "John K.C. Chan",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/171/1449.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/171/thumb_1449.jpg"
  },
  {
